      "post": {
        "description": "Ask a follow-up, and answer it from the research (`REQ-CONV-001`).\n\nAnswered synchronously, unlike a research run. A question against evidence\nalready gathered is one model call, and pushing it through `run_steps`\nwould make the reader wait on a poll for something that takes a second.\n\n**Follow-up research is the exception, and it is deliberately not done\nhere.** `REQ-CONV-003` requires fresh retrieval when the evidence is\ninsufficient, and retrieval belongs to the pipeline \u2014 it needs the budget,\nthe tool registry, the termination gate and the activity stream, none of\nwhich a request handler should own. So the intent is classified, the answer\nsays plainly that new research is needed, and enqueuing that run is the\nnext piece of work. Answering \"I researched that\" without having done so\nwould be the one thing this product must never do.",
        "operationId": "ask_v1_research__session_id__messages_post",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "in": "path",
            "name": "session_id",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "format": "uuid",
              "title": "Session Id",
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          {
            "in": "cookie",
            "name": "scrapr_session",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                {
                  "type": "null"
                }
              ],
              "title": "Scrapr Session"
            }
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
